  "description_short": "Friendly neighbourhood coffee shop in George Central serving quality brews and light meals with genuine warmth.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into York Street in George Central, Ground Control Coffee Shop has earned its reputation as a reliable local favourite. The café strikes that comfortable balance between quality coffee culture and unpretentious neighbourhood hangout, where regulars and visitors alike feel equally welcome.\n\nThe menu covers the essentials well — properly made coffee, fresh pastries, and light meals that suit breakfast through to lunch. The space works for quick takeaways, leisurely catch-ups, or getting some work done over a second cup. It's the kind of place that does the basics right without overcomplicating things.\n\nLocated on one of George's main streets, it's easy to find and convenient for a break while exploring the town centre. The consistent Google rating reflects what keeps people coming back: decent coffee, friendly service, and a welcoming atmosphere that doesn't try too hard.",
